# CODEOWNERS for de-otio/.github — task D3.
# Copied from dot-work/scripts/CODEOWNERS.template; only the repo-specific
# block at the bottom differs per repo, on purpose.
#
# Three things that must not change:
#   1. Catch-all first — CODEOWNERS is last-match-wins, so a later or absent
#      catch-all leaves paths with no owner (finding S5).
#   2. No `<slug>[bot]` anywhere — a bot is a different principal than its
#      operator; a bot owner would let one human plus their own agent
#      satisfy review.
#   3. Owner is `@de-otio/founders`, which GitHub resolves in CODEOWNERS only
#      if the team has explicit write access to this repo — the grant is
#      the control, nothing asserts the owner resolves.
#
# Today this DEFINES ownership without REQUIRING review: rulesets keep
# `require_code_owner_review: false` while the org has one filled seat (see
# dot-work rulesets/README.md, "The N=1 policy").

# --- catch-all: first rule, always ----------------------------------------
*                       @de-otio/founders

# --- agent control plane (finding S10) ------------------------------------
/.mcp.json              @de-otio/founders
/.claude/               @de-otio/founders
/.devcontainer/         @de-otio/founders
/.vscode/               @de-otio/founders
/AGENTS.md              @de-otio/founders

# --- CI and the gate plane ------------------------------------------------
/.github/               @de-otio/founders

